CODEGEN.md §3.4, §3.5, DECISIONS 388: a parameter that is a standard macro and also the name of a type its signature uses is reported as E8011 at the parameter, and not again as E8005 at the same span (the enum's own name is E8011 too).
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A choice.
enum NULL { one, two }

/// Picks a weight.
export fn pick(NULL: NULL) -> Int { return 1 }

emit cpp { out: "@features/a/cpp", namespace: "a", mode: baked }
-- findings.txt --
error[E8011]  a/a.canon:4:6
  NULL, the C++ name derived for a.NULL, is a macro of the C++ standard library

error[E8011]  a/a.canon:7:16
  NULL, the C++ name derived for a.pick.NULL, is a macro of the C++ standard library

2 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
